---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - LibreDB Studio"
  description="Privacy Policy for LibreDB Studio. Learn how we handle cookies, analytics data, and your privacy rights under GDPR."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-24 pb-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="mb-2 text-3xl font-bold text-bright sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mb-12 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: March 1, 2026</p>

      <!-- Introduction -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Introduction</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg">
          LibreDB Studio ("we", "our", or "us") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains
          how we collect, use, and protect information when you visit our website at
          <a
            href="https://libredb.org"
            class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary-bright"
            >libredb.org</a
          >. LibreDB Studio is an open-source project and this website serves as its landing page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Information We Collect -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg">
          We do not require you to create an account or provide personal information to use this
          website. The only data we collect is through analytics cookies, and only if you give your
          consent.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg">
          When you consent to analytics, the following services may collect data:
        </p>
        <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2 text-lg font-medium text-bright">Google Analytics</h3>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg">Google Analytics may collect:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-inside list-disc space-y-2 text-fg">
          <li>Pages visited and time spent on each page</li>
          <li>Referring website or source</li>
          <li>Browser type and operating system</li>
          <li>Approximate geographic location (country/city level)</li>
          <li>Device type (desktop, mobile, tablet)</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-medium text-bright">Meta (Facebook) Pixel</h3>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg">When you accept cookies, Meta Pixel may collect:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-inside list-disc space-y-2 text-fg">
          <li>Pages visited (PageView events)</li>
          <li>Browser and device information</li>
          <li>Approximate geographic location</li>
          <li>Referring URL</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-fg">
          This data is processed by Meta under their
          <a
            href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary-bright"
            >Privacy Policy</a
          >. Meta Pixel is only loaded after you explicitly accept cookies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Cookies -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg">
          Cookies are small text files stored on your device. Below is a summary of the cookies used
          on this site:
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-edge">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-panel text-xs tracking-wider text-fg uppercase">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-3">Cookie</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3">Provider</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3">Purpose</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3">Duration</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-edge">
              <tr class="bg-panel">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-fg">_ga</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Google Analytics</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Distinguishes unique visitors</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">2 years</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-canvas">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-fg">_ga_*</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Google Analytics</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Maintains session state</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">2 years</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-panel">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-fg">_fbp</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Meta (Facebook) Pixel</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Stores and tracks visits across websites</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">3 months</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-canvas">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-fg">fr</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Meta (Facebook) Pixel</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Enables ad delivery and measurement</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">3 months</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">
          We also store your cookie consent preference in <code
            class="rounded bg-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-primary">localStorage</code
          >
          (key: <code class="rounded bg-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-primary"
            >libredb-cookie-consent</code
          >). This is not a cookie and is not sent to any server.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Your Choices -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Your Choices</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg">
          When you first visit our site, a cookie consent banner will appear. You can choose to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-2 text-fg">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bright">Accept</strong> &mdash; analytics cookies will be set and Google
            Analytics will load.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bright">Decline</strong> &mdash; no analytics cookies will be set and
            Google Analytics will not load.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg">
          You can change your preference at any time by clearing your browser's local storage for
          this site and reloading the page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Data Sharing -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Data Sharing</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg">
          If you accept analytics cookies, anonymized usage data is processed by Google Analytics
          under Google's <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary-bright"
            >Privacy Policy</a
          >. We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with any other third parties.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Data Retention -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Data Retention</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg">
          Google Analytics data is retained for 14 months, after which it is automatically deleted.
          Your consent preference stored in local storage persists until you clear it manually.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- GDPR Rights -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Your Rights Under GDPR</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg">
          If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), you have the following rights:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-2 text-fg">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bright">Right to access</strong> &mdash; request a copy of the data we
            hold about you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bright">Right to rectification</strong> &mdash; request correction of
            inaccurate data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bright">Right to erasure</strong> &mdash; request deletion of your data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bright">Right to restrict processing</strong> &mdash; request that we
            limit how we use your data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bright">Right to data portability</strong> &mdash; request your data in
            a machine-readable format.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bright">Right to object</strong> &mdash; object to our processing of your
            data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bright">Right to withdraw consent</strong> &mdash; withdraw your consent
            at any time by clearing local storage.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Children's Privacy -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg">
          This website is not directed at children under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal
          data from children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Changes to This Policy -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg">
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page
          with an updated "Last updated" date. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-bright">Contact</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg">
          If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please open an issue on our
          <a
            href="https://github.com/libredb/libredb-studio/issues"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary-bright"
            >GitHub repository</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Back to Home -->
      <div class="border-t border-edge pt-6">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-primary transition-colors hover:text-primary-bright"
        >
          <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
          </svg>
          Back to Home
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
